# tests/caos-conversation, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating
# this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it records a conversation with `caos mcp hook`, as Claude Code
# does, then reads it back through std/caos-conversation's image to pin how a
# long conversation is paged and cut: from/to, only, msg-width, and the header.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/cli-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=.
